Subject: Tweak: match replays, through the game's own input recorder
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

The retail game keeps a developer's input recorder (NetworkInputRecording)
that no menu reaches: every local match's loading calls StartSinglePlayerGame,
which gives the match a fresh seed and hands the recorder its setup
(RecordedGameConfig); for every fixed step the router (SimpleInputRouter::
OnInputReady) then writes each machine's packet: remap angle, the match's
checksum, frame and seed, the deterministic events and every player's
PackedDetInput record. Played back (mPlaybackEnabled at the loading,
PlaybackRecordedGame), the router reads those packets instead of the pads
(ProcessPlaybackFrame), the Mega Strike and visibility messages come from the
recording, and the steps can run faster (g_numPacketPlaybackTurbo).

The recorder wrote to a file of the console's debug folder through
nlOpenFileDebug. Here its writes and reads go to the port
(src/platform/match_replay.cpp, include/mscharged_replay.h), which keeps the
match in a compact replay file and decides what it records: offline matches
(Domination, Training, the Cup's) but no online, demo or challenge matches.
The recorder is on when the port says so (InitializeNetworkInputRecording).

A replay starts from the title, as Training's match does (Skip intro passes
the title): the title takes the port's start instead of the main menu, and
the port sets the recorded mode, teams, stadium, sides, settings and cheats
without the save and pushes the loading, where PlaybackRecordedGame reads
the recorded seed and setup. After the loading chose the difficulty the port
notes it (recording) or sets the recorded one again (replay).

The recorded checksum, frame and seed are compared by the port, which reports
a difference itself: the router's own check (CheckSyncMismatch) gets the
game's values, so a replay that differs plays on instead of raising the
network error popup of that check.

Off (the port records nothing and plays no replay), the recorder stays as in
the original game. The guarded hooks exist only in the opt-in native game
module.

